To: Sofie Peeters
Subject: RE: Stock in Q after delivery without certificates - how to release

Sure. The Q stock is not an error. With this material the system creates an i=
nspection lot automatically at goods receipt (inspection type 01), and the st=
ock stays blocked in quality inspection until a usage decision is made. Steps=
 below.

The 3 days in September came from two things: the supplier only sent the cert=
ificates on the Wednesday, and QA was not told that the lot existed, so the u=
sage decision was only made on the Thursday. So the trick is to tell QA on da=
y 1 and chase the supplier at the same time.

Step | T-code | What to do | Who
1 | MMBE | Check that the stock really is in Q (quality inspection) for plant=
 2030 | Warehouse
2 | QA32 | Find the inspection lot by plant, material or PO and note the lot =
number | Warehouse
3 | - | Ask the supplier for the certificates; mail the lot number to QA | Wa=
rehouse
4 | QE51N | Record results of the QA checks and attach the certificates | QA
5 | QA11 | Make the usage decision (code A =3D accepted) | QA
6 | MMBE | Check that the stock moved from Q to unrestricted | Warehouse

Kind regards,
Lukas Becker
SAP key user SD/LE
Corp Europe B.V. | Rotterdam
T +31 10 680 5342

